      {
        "variation": "default",
        "version": "initial",
        "items": [
          {
            "question": "What is the difference between chest regulation and smARTvalve?",
            "answer": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The standard Decap system regulates pressure for the complete chest, so all active pipes follow the same pressure movement. smARTvalve controls every pipe independently, giving each note its own pressure, articulation and dynamics.",
                "spans": [],
                "direction": "ltr"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "question": "Which pressure effects are available?",
            "answer": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Depending on the selected system, effects include crescendo, decrescendo, pitch and modulation movement, LFO vibrato, tremolo, slope, decay and shaped note articulation. smARTvalve can apply expression independently to each pipe.",
                "spans": [],
                "direction": "ltr"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "question": "How can a Pipes system be built?",
            "answer": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "text": "It can be integrated into a traditional organ or orchestrion façade, built as a compact cube or pedestal, mounted in a transportable frame or flight case, added to an existing organ, or developed as a fully custom installation.",
                "spans": [],
                "direction": "ltr"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
